## 2. Engineering & UX Mandates

- **No-Dead-Button Mandate**: Every button, link, and interactive element MUST have an active handler (`onClick`, router navigation, modal trigger, or form submission).
- **6 Mandatory UI States**: Every screen and table must handle: (1) Default/Success, (2) Loading Skeleton, (3) Empty State, (4) Validation/Error, (5) Responsive, (6) Interactive/Focus.
- **Zero Dummy Text**: Consume `docs/domain-lexicon.md`. Never use "Lorem Ipsum" or generic dummy labels.
- **Verification Gate**: No task is marked DONE without running tests via `bash scripts/verify-task.sh [TASK-ID]`.
- **Safety Gate**: NEVER execute `git commit` or `git push` automatically.


- Theme-ready UI rule: no hardcoded colors/fonts in components; use only Tailwind/CSS tokens from tailwind.config.ts and globals.css, reuse src/components/ui, keep logic out of views. Full redesign comes later. See AGENTS.md "Theme-Ready UI Rule".
